course: dictionary
lesson: 13593
title: Inconsistent: changing, clashing, unfair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inconsistent is built from in- (not) and consistent (staying the same). So inconsistent means not staying the same from one time to the next. Look at the clues around it. «Ben scored three goals on Monday, none on Wednesday and five on Friday. He is an inconsistent player.» His scores keep changing, so inconsistent means changing.
explain: The word can also mean that two things do not agree. «The witness said the thief wore a red coat, but the camera shows a blue one. Her story is inconsistent with the video.» The story and the video do not fit together, so they cannot both be true. Try the swap: "her story does not match the video" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Use the noun inconsistency for the thing itself: «There was an inconsistency in the test results.» A rule can be inconsistent too: «The teacher gave me a star one day and a telling-off the next for the same thing.» That means the rule was not applied the same way each time.
fact: Inconsistent means not staying the same, changing from one time to the next.
fact: Inconsistent can also mean not agreeing or fitting together with something else.
fact: «Inconsistent with» means does not match: «The clues are inconsistent with his story.»
fact: «Inconsistent» can mean not following the same rules each time, as in «inconsistent marking».
fact: The opposite of inconsistent is consistent, which means steady and the same every time.
exercise: «Mia's spelling is inconsistent: perfect on Monday, wrong on Tuesday.» What does inconsistent mean here? | *Not staying the same from day to day | Very long | Always correct | Written in pencil
exercise: «The map is inconsistent with the sign at the gate.» What does inconsistent with mean? | Exactly the same as | *Does not match or agree with | Painted in the same colour as | Next to
exercise: Copy the noun form of inconsistent from this sentence: «The inconsistency in the results worried the scientist.» | *inconsistency | worried | scientist | results
test: Dad says, «Your rule is inconsistent: you can stay up on Friday but not on Saturday, for the same reason.» What is the problem? | The rule is written in a book | *The rule is not applied the same way each time | You are too tall to stay up | Friday is always later than Saturday
test: «The two facts are inconsistent, so they cannot both be true.» Which statement is right? | The two facts are very loud | The two facts are both exactly the same | *The two facts do not agree with each other | The two facts are long
exam: Which sentence uses inconsistent correctly? | «I was inconsistent and went to bed early.» | «The sandwich was inconsistent with a glass of milk.» | *«The wind was inconsistent: strong, then almost gone, then strong again.» | «The inconsistent dog slept under the table all day.»
